(2835384, 393302, 5354, '<td valign="top">Haha I know exactly where this is, and I know what your title refers to <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=161870" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/322/thumb/161870.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/322/thumb/161870.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/322/thumb/161870.jpg"/></a>;-)<br/> <br/>Nice one, I think the blue sky and sun is not quite so dramatic as the original by Ed, nor as atmospheric as the misty weather we enjoyed at our get together. We must do that again sometime. All the same its a good image, nicely set up and executed.<br/> <br/>Now is this John or Pauline I wonder?</td>', 'Haha I know exactly where this is, and I know what your title refers to ;-) Nice one, I think the blue sky and sun is not quite so dramatic as the original by Ed, nor as atmospheric as the misty weather we enjoyed at our get together. We must do that again sometime. All the same its a good image, nicely set up and executed. Now is this John or Pauline I wonder?', '2006-09-14 17:22:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835447, 394222, 57936, '<td valign="top">If the tree were not chopped off this would get higher marks. As a shot with a single tree as the subject, it is incomplete. Great colors and wonderful locale!</td>', 'If the tree were not chopped off this would get higher marks. As a shot with a single tree as the subject, it is incomplete. Great colors and wonderful locale!', '2006-09-14 17:45:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835448, 392613, 65540, '<td valign="top">Brilliant colorsnicely done.</td>', 'Brilliant colorsnicely done.', '2006-09-14 17:45:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835452, 394312, 57936, '<td valign="top">Nice, but it took too long to find the tree. The ravine is the salient feature of the image, not the tree. (At least to me...) Also, the sky looks like you cloned out a bunch of stuff and made an artificial horizon. Not that that is out of bounds for an advanced editing challenge, but it doesn''t look right to me... more like some wierd fog was approaching than a true sky.</td>', 'Nice, but it took too long to find the tree. The ravine is the salient feature of the image, not the tree. (At least to me...) Also, the sky looks like you cloned out a bunch of stuff and made an artificial horizon. Not that that is out of bounds for an advanced editing challenge, but it doesn''t look right to me... more like some wierd fog was approaching than a true sky.', '2006-09-14 17:48:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835484, 393019, 49366, '<td valign="top">beautiful!</td>', 'beautiful!', '2006-09-14 18:00:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835488, 394508, 57936, '<td valign="top">Too little is in focus and it it too dark. I expect that the twig is a tree, but you cannot tell because the bottom of it is entirely lost in the background. Longer DOF and more contrast in the foreground would help.</td>', 'Too little is in focus and it it too dark. I expect that the twig is a tree, but you cannot tell because the bottom of it is entirely lost in the background. Longer DOF and more contrast in the foreground would help.', '2006-09-14 18:01:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835499, 393972, 57936, '<td valign="top">I see that the tree is straight, but that should not be done at the expense of the horizon. Also, the dodge on the background is too extreme. It makes it look washed out and distracting. If you wanted to de-emphasize the background detail, I would suggest using burn to darken it. Bright areas tend to draw the eye and distract.</td>', 'I see that the tree is straight, but that should not be done at the expense of the horizon. Also, the dodge on the background is too extreme. It makes it look washed out and distracting. If you wanted to de-emphasize the background detail, I would suggest using burn to darken it. Bright areas tend to draw the eye and distract.', '2006-09-14 18:04:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835505, 394520, 57936, '<td valign="top">The tree is bearly visible against the background. The bright rocks and sky fooled your camera''s light meter into into thinking the scene was better lit than it is. It would be better to use spot metering on the tree and then adjust the sky later if it is too blown-out.</td>', 'The tree is bearly visible against the background. The bright rocks and sky fooled your camera''s light meter into into thinking the scene was better lit than it is. It would be better to use spot metering on the tree and then adjust the sky later if it is too blown-out.', '2006-09-14 18:07:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835516, 394514, 57936, '<td valign="top">I would argue that the child, not the tree, is the main subject of this image. If the tree were the main subject it would not be cut off...</td>', 'I would argue that the child, not the tree, is the main subject of this image. If the tree were the main subject it would not be cut off...', '2006-09-14 18:11:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835518, 394513, 45475, '<td valign="top">My first impression was that this is overexposed. But on closer inspection, I see it''s the post work. Still not quite sure what to make of it. Feels a little too hard and rough, particularly the clouds. 5 for now, but I''ll come back for another look once I''m done voting on all. <i>ok, bumping</i></td>', 'My first impression was that this is overexposed. But on closer inspection, I see it''s the post work. Still not quite sure what to make of it. Feels a little too hard and rough, particularly the clouds. 5 for now, but I''ll come back for another look once I''m done voting on all. ok, bumping', '2006-09-14 18:11:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835521, 393808, 57936, '<td valign="top">Where did you find Autumn Leaves during this challenge?????</td>', 'Where did you find Autumn Leaves during this challenge?????', '2006-09-14 18:12:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835528, 394388, 57936, '<td valign="top">I like this in some ways and don''t in others. The exagerated Panoramic view is a bit wierd, though I can see what you were getting at with it. The tree really does stand out nicely with all the blown-out sky and the dark ground, but the out of focus and totally black area at the front end of the foreground should be cropped out IMO.</td>', 'I like this in some ways and don''t in others. The exagerated Panoramic view is a bit wierd, though I can see what you were getting at with it. The tree really does stand out nicely with all the blown-out sky and the dark ground, but the out of focus and totally black area at the front end of the foreground should be cropped out IMO.', '2006-09-14 18:16:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835534, 393825, 57936, '<td valign="top">I see where you''re going, but it would be more effective with less negative space in the sky. Maybe a pano? Still: 9</td>', 'I see where you''re going, but it would be more effective with less negative space in the sky. Maybe a pano? Still: 9', '2006-09-14 18:18:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835536, 391670, 57936, '<td valign="top">looks over-sharpenned to me. The leaves look funky against the sky...</td>', 'looks over-sharpenned to me. The leaves look funky against the sky...', '2006-09-14 18:19:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835537, 394248, 45475, '<td valign="top">Hmmm... slightly oversharpened, the shadows are a little murky and the sky is badly overexposed on the top-left. But, I do like composition. You''ve managed to isolate the tree from the rest, well done.</td>', 'Hmmm... slightly oversharpened, the shadows are a little murky and the sky is badly overexposed on the top-left. But, I do like composition. You''ve managed to isolate the tree from the rest, well done.', '2006-09-14 18:19:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835540, 394457, 57936, '<td valign="top">The single tree doesn''t stand out enough against the background trees. The bottom of the trunk and the top of the tree are ok, but the middle gets lost in the green behind it. I also would like it better with the tree offset.</td>', 'The single tree doesn''t stand out enough against the background trees. The bottom of the trunk and the top of the tree are ok, but the middle gets lost in the green behind it. I also would like it better with the tree offset.', '2006-09-14 18:20:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835543, 394229, 57936, '<td valign="top">I would suggest that the dog is the subject here, not the tree, which is cut off. The bright sky and muted tones nicely depict the dream quality, but it doesn''t present the tree ideally.</td>', 'I would suggest that the dog is the subject here, not the tree, which is cut off. The bright sky and muted tones nicely depict the dream quality, but it doesn''t present the tree ideally.', '2006-09-14 18:22:16.000000', NULL, 1),
