(2846211, 392964, 20168, '<td valign="top">Here''s the shot I took the same night as "The Wedding Tree", while I was standing next to Robert (Bear_Music). I took it with an old Sony Mavica digital which currently cannot store EXIF data on the memory card (a floppy disk), so I didn''t enter to challenge for fear of being DQ''d. The evening light faded quickly behind a high cloud bank out over the Pacific. Nonetheless, time at Ecola Point overlooking the Big Blue is always a gift! It was good to spend time with Robert Ward (Bear_Music), Steve Davidson and Jason Friesen (DrAchoo) at our home in Cannon Beach. Congrats Robt on 15!<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=394705" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/20168/thumb/394705.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/20168/thumb/394705.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/20168/thumb/394705.jpg"/></a> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-18 21:39:55.</i></td>', 'Here''s the shot I took the same night as "The Wedding Tree", while I was standing next to Robert (Bear_Music). I took it with an old Sony Mavica digital which currently cannot store EXIF data on the memory card (a floppy disk), so I didn''t enter to challenge for fear of being DQ''d. The evening light faded quickly behind a high cloud bank out over the Pacific. Nonetheless, time at Ecola Point overlooking the Big Blue is always a gift! It was good to spend time with Robert Ward (Bear_Music), Steve Davidson and Jason Friesen (DrAchoo) at our home in Cannon Beach. Congrats Robt on 15! ', '2006-09-18 22:38:06.000000', '2006-09-18 22:39:55.000000', 0),
