(2847386, 394537, 23913, '<td valign="top">primary "processing"/cause of blur - winds from south east @ 18-22mph<br/> <br/>had to leave the shutter open for the light and i got the blur as well. wasn''t counting on it but i kinda liked it. otherwise photo is as is with a little color adj. and downsize of corse.<br/> <br/>thanks all for the comments just thought i would explain.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-19 11:05:58.</i></td>', 'primary "processing"/cause of blur - winds from south east @ 18-22mph had to leave the shutter open for the light and i got the blur as well. wasn''t counting on it but i kinda liked it. otherwise photo is as is with a little color adj. and downsize of corse. thanks all for the comments just thought i would explain.', '2006-09-19 12:05:15.000000', '2006-09-19 12:05:58.000000', 0),
(2847394, 393905, 3724, '<td valign="top">I would agree w/ previous comments - can''t miss that the vote placement for this one is curious.</td>', 'I would agree w/ previous comments - can''t miss that the vote placement for this one is curious.', '2006-09-19 12:11:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2847549, 391320, 49155, '<td valign="top">Post voting: I have read here that others think the photo is not straight horizontally that is - what crap! If viewers actually took the time they would see that the foreground is a hill sloping down to the left and there is a view of the true horizon behind it which is quite level.<br/> <br/>PS: where is this kite everyone is talking about?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-19 12:24:07.</i></td>', 'Post voting: I have read here that others think the photo is not straight horizontally that is - what crap! If viewers actually took the time they would see that the foreground is a hill sloping down to the left and there is a view of the true horizon behind it which is quite level. PS: where is this kite everyone is talking about?', '2006-09-19 13:22:59.000000', '2006-09-19 13:24:07.000000', 0),
(2847567, 394458, 49155, '<td valign="top">Post voting: Another photo where the public thought the horizon was out of  kilt - not right, sorry! It is a hill sloping down to the left, one only has to look at the angles in the fence and the grass to see that.</td>', 'Post voting: Another photo where the public thought the horizon was out of  kilt - not right, sorry! It is a hill sloping down to the left, one only has to look at the angles in the fence and the grass to see that.', '2006-09-19 13:31:16.000000', NULL, 0),
