(2847583, 394025, 42100, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a top ten &amp; PB!  Glad to see you finally get a score you deserve(way to many undeserved low scores on the doll series).</td>', 'Congrats on a top ten & PB!  Glad to see you finally get a score you deserve(way to many undeserved low scores on the doll series).', '2006-09-19 13:38:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2847612, 393701, 30982, '<td valign="top">''Tis a good "average DPC" shot - aka much better than the average person would shoot, but only average for DPC and not as good as you''re used to.  I''m not entirely sure I like the balance - the tree takes too much space to be "minimalistic".  I''m thinking a long horizontal shot might be the ticket, though obviously not possible from the way this was framed.</td>', '''Tis a good "average DPC" shot - aka much better than the average person would shoot, but only average for DPC and not as good as you''re used to.  I''m not entirely sure I like the balance - the tree takes too much space to be "minimalistic".  I''m thinking a long horizontal shot might be the ticket, though obviously not possible from the way this was framed.', '2006-09-19 14:01:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2847700, 394530, 53147, '<td valign="top">I gave a 6 on this one. I like the shot in general but I think with some more processing and tweaking you really could have had a much stronger shot. The colors are a bit flat and the lighting a bit dark. Play with curves a bit and up the saturation and I think you would have a more DPC friendly shot.<br/> <br/>Edit - I just did a quick edit of it. Give me a shout if I can post it somewhere.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-19 13:57:09.</i></td>', 'I gave a 6 on this one. I like the shot in general but I think with some more processing and tweaking you really could have had a much stronger shot. The colors are a bit flat and the lighting a bit dark. Play with curves a bit and up the saturation and I think you would have a more DPC friendly shot. Edit - I just did a quick edit of it. Give me a shout if I can post it somewhere.', '2006-09-19 14:53:04.000000', '2006-09-19 14:57:09.000000', 0),
(2847713, 394256, 53147, '<td valign="top">Nice twist on the challenge. Good to see something other than those stupid tree silhouettes against sunset skies that were way overdone inthis challenge ;)  This shot didnt grab me right away. The abstract nature was good to separate yours from the other shots but the pic seems jumbled (not that you had any control over the tree). Interesting colors and textures but it just seems to be lacking something that I cant quite put my finger on.</td>', 'Nice twist on the challenge. Good to see something other than those stupid tree silhouettes against sunset skies that were way overdone inthis challenge ;)  This shot didnt grab me right away. The abstract nature was good to separate yours from the other shots but the pic seems jumbled (not that you had any control over the tree). Interesting colors and textures but it just seems to be lacking something that I cant quite put my finger on.', '2006-09-19 15:04:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2847720, 394372, 53147, '<td valign="top">Nice shot BeeCee - underrated IMO.</td>', 'Nice shot BeeCee - underrated IMO.', '2006-09-19 15:07:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2847732, 393990, 53147, '<td valign="top">Once again a nice shot with your daughter in it. Way to go on scoring well even though its "another kid shot" (as the critics would say).</td>', 'Once again a nice shot with your daughter in it. Way to go on scoring well even though its "another kid shot" (as the critics would say).', '2006-09-19 15:12:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2847881, 393443, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review:<br/> <br/>Focus is good.<br/> <br/>Color, saturation and hue are good as well.  <br/> <br/>The positon and angle of the tree leads the eye out and off the top left of the frame.  The overly large ornament competes for attention.  If the story being told is that the ornament caused the crash, then the debris around the tree is OK.  I assume the tree is not being discarded, at the title tallks about being too soon.<br/> <br/>The red backdrop postioned where it is, leaves exposed white wall that also is distracting.  There isn''t enough there in this view to really tell us that the tree caused the wall to be exposed.  <br/> <br/>The picture is nice and sharp, and you did a good job with the depth of field.</td>', 'Critique Club Review: Focus is good. Color, saturation and hue are good as well.   The positon and angle of the tree leads the eye out and off the top left of the frame.  The overly large ornament competes for attention.  If the story being told is that the ornament caused the crash, then the debris around the tree is OK.  I assume the tree is not being discarded, at the title tallks about being too soon. The red backdrop postioned where it is, leaves exposed white wall that also is distracting.  There isn''t enough there in this view to really tell us that the tree caused the wall to be exposed.   The picture is nice and sharp, and you did a good job with the depth of field.', '2006-09-19 16:12:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(2847934, 394164, 3569, '<td valign="top">FYI,<br/> <br/>Some folks here in Colorado predict heavy snow winters by the loss of pine needles.  The orange needles will be lost prior to winter.  Heavy snows and lots of needles mean broken tree branches. So the trees somehow know (God''s great creation) when a heavy snow winters will occur and they drop some of their needles before winter (lessen the load).  This is a healthy ponderosa Pine.  That''s why I titled the shot, so you can learn non-photo fun stuff too.  Van</td>', 'FYI, Some folks here in Colorado predict heavy snow winters by the loss of pine needles.  The orange needles will be lost prior to winter.  Heavy snows and lots of needles mean broken tree branches. So the trees somehow know (God''s great creation) when a heavy snow winters will occur and they drop some of their needles before winter (lessen the load).  This is a healthy ponderosa Pine.  That''s why I titled the shot, so you can learn non-photo fun stuff too.  Van', '2006-09-19 16:54:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2848207, 394247, 38234, '<td valign="top">A belated congratulations on this fine win!!  Really well done!!  800 km - wow!!!!!!!</td>', 'A belated congratulations on this fine win!!  Really well done!!  800 km - wow!!!!!!!', '2006-09-19 18:27:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2848460, 392897, 47852, '<td valign="top">Hey, congrats Neil!  I really need to get back out to Thatcher to get a shot of this tree... everyone else keeps getting these amazing shots of it!  Way to go! :)</td>', 'Hey, congrats Neil!  I really need to get back out to Thatcher to get a shot of this tree... everyone else keeps getting these amazing shots of it!  Way to go! :)', '2006-09-19 20:00:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(2848592, 394458, 29177, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by szalona:</b></div><hr/><i> crooked horixon doesnt feel like it works here. title doesnt work very well either in my opinion though i must say if it were straightened i think its an awesome photo.  i like the fence.. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Horizon is not crooked... it is a HILL! Titles are subjective... I thought we were voting on the photograph...</td>', 'Originally posted by szalona: crooked horixon doesnt feel like it works here. title doesnt work very well either in my opinion though i must say if it were straightened i think its an awesome photo.  i like the fence..   Horizon is not crooked... it is a HILL! Titles are subjective... I thought we were voting on the photograph...', '2006-09-19 20:45:39.000000', NULL, 0),
